Terminal progress: request-level reading, prefill, answering, and done lines.

VLLM_TERMINAL_PROGRESS=1 opts into per-request server console output. Logs
completed prompt chunks (excluding in-flight async work), per-request prefill
rate with cached tokens separated, one answering line per second, and finish
or cancellation summaries. Output contains request IDs and counts, never text.
No CUDA synchronization and no changes to requests, sampling or API responses.
The Turing launcher enables this and tees its server log to logs/turing.log.

The output format is modeled on Project Maya (https://github.com/mw00/project-maya, MIT, Peasant Smith and the Project Maya contributors).

Re-cut against 0.33.0: in the output processor, the progress call now follows 0.33's new
streaming_chunk_boundary assignment, just before step 4.

